From a153b33de4724b662c90efad19767118ceead0f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sanjeev Kumar Paul <sanjeevkumarpaul25@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 10:59:09 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Restyle: "Bone & Floodlight" type and colour system
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Type: Fraunces (display; SOFT 40, WONK 1, optical sizing, sentence
  case, light weights), Manrope (UI/body, 1.6 leading, 68ch), JetBrains
  Mono (uppercase tracked labels, data, counters). Fluid 1.2→1.25 scale;
  display clamp(2.75rem, 6vw, 5.5rem). Drops Barlow Condensed and Inter.
- Colour: warm neutrals (bone/sand/taupe/umber/espresso/ink), champagne +
  bronze metal for focal marks and keylines, ochre ≤5%, graphite night
  sections. No pure black/white. Semantic tokens (--bg, --surface, --text,
  --accent, --em, --cta...) with a .theme-night override; components
  renamed off colour-named variables.
- Material: SVG grain overlay, diagonal window-light on bone walls, inner
  light instead of drop shadows, conic champagne sheen on primary CTAs.
- Charts re-validated for the bone surface (all series ≥3:1); heatmap ramp
  sand → forest.
- 3D scene and mascots inherit the palette: bone/brick draw ball, forest
  scoresheet ball with ochre panels, espresso "seven" ball with champagne
  panels, champagne rim light and atmosphere, bronze satellites.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PtuBR2ekwFULQyM2MqFBuU
